        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$27$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}4^{3\\log_4(3)}&=\\left(4^{\\log_4(3)}\\right)^3\\\\4^{3\\log_4(3)}&=3^3\\\\4^{3\\log_4(3)}&=27\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q113",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$25^{\\log_5(4)}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$16$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}25^{\\log_5(4)}&=(5^2)^{\\log_5(4)}\\\\25^{\\log_5(4)}&=\\left(5^{\\log_5(4)}\\right)^2\\\\25^{\\log_5(4)}&=4^2\\\\25^{\\log_5(4)}&=16\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q114",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$3^{\\log_{27}(a)}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt[3]{a}$, for $a>0$.",
          "worked": "The logarithm requires $a>0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}3^{\\log_{27}(a)}&=(27^{1/3})^{\\log_{27}(a)}\\\\3^{\\log_{27}(a)}&=\\left(27^{\\log_{27}(a)}\\right)^{1/3}\\\\3^{\\log_{27}(a)}&=a^{1/3}\\\\3^{\\log_{27}(a)}&=\\sqrt[3]{a}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q115",
        "type": "part",
