          "worked": "For the original logarithm to be defined, $a>0$, $a\\ne1$, $n\\ne0$ and $x>0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a^{\\log_{a^n}(x)}&=\\left((a^n)^{1/n}\\right)^{\\log_{a^n}(x)}\\\\a^{\\log_{a^n}(x)}&=\\left((a^n)^{\\log_{a^n}(x)}\\right)^{1/n}\\\\a^{\\log_{a^n}(x)}&=x^{1/n}\\end{align*}$$",
